Cover what the review found untested in the carry-over scheduler

A post-implementation reviewer ran 45 mutations against 89c927a; 10
survived the whole suite, 6 of them also the differential test at its
default 64 cases. Each gap now has a test, checked again on the current
code to fail under the mutation it targets:

- a_voice_ends_with_the_last_sound_of_a_play_that_loaded: no release of
  the voice hold after a successful start (every voice would live
  forever, undoing "finished sounds leave their voice").
- a_voice_stays_open_while_a_second_play_into_it_loads: a hold released
  twice. remove_loading_play also debug-asserts it is releasing a hold
  it has (letting_go_of_a_loading_play_twice_is_caught), so a double
  release fails loudly in every debug test.
- a_stop_that_cancels_a_play_aborts_its_load: no abort on cancel (the
  load would keep a slot until it finished or timed out).
- fadeall_cancels_a_play_still_loading: fadeall not cancelling. fadeall
  is also added to the differential test's generator.
- voice_fade_out_reaching_only_a_loading_play_succeeds,
  a_play_rejected_by_the_load_limit_holds_no_voice,
  a_speed_for_a_streamed_voice_does_not_carry_onto_a_play_into_it, and
  a_stop_cancelling_an_mqtt_play_logs_why (the reason troubleshooting.md
  quotes).

Tests made stronger:
- a_speed_ignored_with_a_warning_reaches_a_loading_play_without_changing_
  it: the play now has its own speed 0.5. Carrying the ignored (-1,
  pitch) used to leave the 1.0 the test expected, because the mixer
  rejects a negative pitch-corrected speed; now the test sees the
  play's speed and pitch mode change.
- scheduler_stopall_cancels_a_load_in_flight: checks the cancelled load
  let go of the cache (it was aborted) instead of only that the task set
  is empty; it fails when no abort happens.
- tests/carry_over_property_test.rs: the one-at-a-time reference used
  the production SampleSelector::matches, the code the scheduler side
  also relies on. It now has its own OR matcher, and disabling file
  matching in SampleSelector fails the property.

Renamed a_stop_cancels_loading_plays_and_stops_playing_sounds_together
to voice_fade_out_cancels_loading_plays_and_fades_playing_sounds_
together, which is what it does.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
and a warning-free release build (RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings);
broker-backed native suite (MQTTAUDIO_BROKER_TESTS=1, TLS CA set) 1042
passed, 0 failed, 7 device-gated ignored. The differential test passed
200 cases with fadeall in the generator.

